# Uniform by-reference capture (F3 — owner-write form, nested-nursery parity guard).
# The critical owner-write-after-spawn case: a closure `f` captures a by-reference local `x` (a cell) and READS
# it; the owner MUTATES that cell (`x[0] = 5`) AFTER `spawn f()`. The task's copy of `f` must snapshot
# `x` at SPAWN time (value `0`), independent of the later owner write. `result` is a
# `Shared[int]` (crosses by reference, an Arc), so the task writes the value it observed back to the
# parent. Nesting `work()` under `main`'s `parallel:` forces the M:N eager nested-nursery path (which
# wires the task at spawn time) — the exact path where a shared-callee serial engine used to read the
# post-write value `5` while M:N read the snapshot `0`. Since the fix, it prints `0`.
import std.concurrency

fn work():
    x := [0]
    result := Shared(0)
    f := fn(): result.set(x[0])
    parallel:
        spawn f()
        x[0] = 5
    print(result.get())         # 0 — task snapshotted x=[0] at spawn

fn main():
    parallel:
        spawn work()

main()
